	Dataphor
	This file is licensed under a modified BSD-license which can be found here: http://dataphor.org/dataphor_license.txt

	Runs device coverage for the PGSQLDevice: the sibling of TestMSSQLDevice, driving the same corpus.

	TestDevice is created by whoever runs this script, not here, as in the sibling: LivePGSQLDeviceTest
	(tests/DAE.Server.Tests) creates it in TestFramework.Coverage.Base against the server the environment variable
	DATAPHOR_TEST_PGSQL names, and D4 has no way to read an environment variable.

	One statement of the sibling is deliberately absent here. That script raises an error naming every catalog object called
	TestFramework.Coverage.Devices.TestDevice-something, which cannot succeed against any device or any version: this
	library's own Logic.d4 creates an operator TestDevice(Name, Integer) whose catalog name is exactly that, so the statement
	always fires and stops the run before the corpus is reached (LiveDeviceTest records it as a known failure, and
	test-pre-3-1-scripts-policy owns whether it may be repaired there). Copying it here would mean writing a new script that
	cannot pass. Nothing else differs.
*/

// Make sure the device is functional and connected
EnsureDeviceStarted('TestDevice');

if not exists (DeviceOperators where Device_Name = ObjectName('TestDevice')) then
	raise Error('TestDevice has no operator maps: the device''s system catalog did not register.');

// reset applicable cases
delete ApplicableDeviceCases;

// Run the tests
TestDevice(ObjectName('TestDevice'), nil);

// If any test failed, throw an error with all the test failure messages.
if exists (DeviceCaseResults where DeviceName = ObjectName('TestDevice') and Status = "Failed") then
	raise
		Error
		(
			Concat
			(
				{ Message, Delimiter }
					from
					(
						DeviceCaseResults
							where DeviceName = ObjectName('TestDevice')
								and Status = "Failed"
							{
								DeviceCase_ID,
								'Device Case ' + DeviceCase_ID.ToString() + ' failed: ' + Results Message,
								ASCII(list(Byte) { 10, 13 }) Delimiter
							}
					)
				order by { DeviceCase_ID }
			)
		);
